summary:
Generative large language models (LLMs) do not have to follow a decoder-only transformer architecture. By integrating masked language models with discrete diffusion, the resulting diffusion language models can excel in both representation learning and generation, and even few-shot learning and reasoning.
Quoting @zaixiang_zheng
@cwolferesearch We explored how to approach a generative BERT-like masked language model as scalable (discrete) diffusion language model, and observed promising results on conditional gen (e.g, MT), instruction-following, ICL and premise of reasoning -

